{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433029-carnivores","id":433029,"title":"Carnivores","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-08T13:30:46-07:00","id":433029,"title":"Carnivores","content":"Strictly speaking, what makes a creature carnivorous enough to be viable to sate Primal Urge restrictions? For instance, most birds will count insects as part of their diets, so could an uratha be properly nourished by a chicken parm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T13:56:57-07:00","id":433087,"title":"","content":"From what I've read, carnivores come in two types: mesocarnivores and hypercarnivores. Mesocarnivores have 50-70% of their diet as meat, while hypercarnviores have a diet consisting of 70%+. From what I can tell, dogs fall into the mesocarnivore group, so your typical Uratha should be aiming to eat creatures around that same amount, to sate their wolfish appetites. If I were an Uratha myself, I would go for creatures that eat 65-70% for my diet, as werewolves appear to have stronger hunting instincts than natural wolves do due to their spiritual natures.<br /> <br /> Edit: Tried to make wording clearer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 03-08-2015, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:01:29-07:00","id":433097,"title":"","content":"A lot of the fish Humans commonly eat are carnivorous. Cod, salmon, haddock... If you're looking for supermarket available stuff for PU 4 and up, there's your best area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:06:04-07:00","id":433100,"title":"","content":"What I mean is, at a certain point an uratha's Primal Urge forces him to eat carnivores in order to avoid bleeding Essence. It's not how <i>much</i> meat an uratha needs to consume that I'm looking for, but rather the <i>quality</i> of the meat eaten. So again, would a sometimes-carnivore like a turkey or chicken fit the bill?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:09:29-07:00","id":433106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433029-carnivores?p=433100#post433100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I mean is, at a certain point an uratha's Primal Urge forces him to eat carnivores in order to avoid bleeding Essence. It's not how <i>much</i> meat an uratha needs to consume that I'm looking for, but rather the <i>quality</i> of the meat eaten. So again, would a sometimes-carnivore like a turkey or chicken fit the bill?</div> </div> </div> </div>A sometimes-carnviore could be seen as the equivalent of eating a chocolate bar and a Monster Energy Drink for breakfast before going off to class: yeah, it can hold you by, but when you don't eat something good for you, boy howdy will you go downhill.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:14:54-07:00","id":433114,"title":"","content":"Cats and dogs are probably the most common in a urban enviroment.<br /> Frogs and spiders as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:20:19-07:00","id":433116,"title":"","content":"I think dogs would technically count as wolves, so there are issues with that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:29:54-07:00","id":433121,"title":"","content":"Considering that before you get to the level of only subsisting on other carnivores, you have to eat raw meat, you'd have to go out and kill the bird itself. I would count birds of prey, but not most common birds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T16:04:36-07:00","id":433259,"title":"","content":"I think the question you need to consider first is:<br /> <br /> Do you want to follow the scientific concept of what makes something a carnivore, or do you want a more symbolic interpretation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T16:09:40-07:00","id":433260,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;predator&quot; would probably be a less confusing term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T16:40:30-07:00","id":433269,"title":"","content":"I think 'if it was easy, we would have a lot more PU 6 Uratha wandering around' so even salmon would be a cop-out. Hot-blooded badasd animals only - birds of prey and creatures which you could stick a 'dire' in front of and have a good sci-fi monster movie about.<br /> <br /> Personally I think if massive prey animals exist in an area (12-point-bucks, elephants, wild boar) they would be awesome enough to be a challenge to satisfy the beast. Otherwise there will be a rash of tiger disappearances at area zoos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T16:48:50-07:00","id":433276,"title":"","content":"More PU 6 Uratha than what? Nothing in the books indicates that they're notably rare or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T16:56:03-07:00","id":433283,"title":"","content":"Eh, more-than-otherwise? Not that any nwod splat is supposed to be even a significant chunk of the population, but I assumed that the higher 'power' stats (blood potency, etc) and the obligations needed to maintain that lifestyle would mean you would have fewer of each as you climb the ranks? I just picked 6 as an arbitrarily-higher number than the 1 characters start as. ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T17:04:18-07:00","id":433295,"title":"","content":"I don't think Uratha would be beholden to human concepts of what makes a &quot;badass&quot; animal anyway. A predator is a predator, and they will respect that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T17:12:46-07:00","id":433302,"title":"","content":"Fair point. By the same token I think they would have a more nuanced conception of what 'worthy' prey is than 'does it eat meat', no? A sufficiently Cunning prey gets respect, like the still-not-defeated beshilu/azlu do...<br /> <br /> I just don't know if I would find it practical (or in-touch with the feel of a game) to hard line 'carnivore' before 'sufficiently impressive to satisfy the barely harnessed force that rules your soul'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T17:15:59-07:00","id":433304,"title":"","content":"Yes, there are after all a lot of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/To_Catch_a_Predator\" target=\"_blank\">predators</a> out there the Forsaken might think of as disgraces to the name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T18:41:14-07:00","id":433396,"title":"","content":"High Primal Urge Uratha are the reason why all the neighborhood stray cats and dogs have been disappearing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}